rtlwifi: rtl_pci: refill the RX slot before releasing it to hardware

In the new_trx_flow RX path, _rtl_pci_rx_interrupt() advances the hardware read
pointer (rtl_write_word to 0x3B4 in new_trx_end) BEFORE it refills the just-freed
buffer descriptor with a new skb (_rtl_pci_init_one_rxdesc under no_new). Between
those two points the descriptor still holds the DMA address of the skb that was
just handed up to mac80211, but the hardware has already been told the slot is
free -- so it may DMA an incoming frame straight into that in-flight skb.

On a fast little-endian host the window is a few instructions and effectively
never loses the race; on this 400 MHz big-endian RTL8196E under sustained RX
(AP mode) it loses it constantly, silently corrupting whatever the skb's memory
is reused for -- presenting as random SIGSEGVs in unrelated processes with no
driver-level error, and as a 100%-softirq lockup once the corruption spreads.

Move the 0x3B4 write to after the refill so the slot is only released to the
hardware once it points at a fresh buffer.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtlwifi/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtlwifi/pci.c
@@ -795,8 +795,6 @@
 					RTL_PCI_MAX_RX_COUNT;
 
 			rx_remained_cnt--;
-			rtl_write_word(rtlpriv, 0x3B4,
-				       rtlpci->rx_ring[hw_queue].next_rx_rp);
 		}
 		if (((rtlpriv->link_info.num_rx_inperiod +
 		      rtlpriv->link_info.num_tx_inperiod) > 8) ||
@@ -811,6 +809,15 @@
 				if (new_skb)
 					dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 			}
+			/* Release the slot to the hardware only AFTER it has been
+			 * refilled with a fresh buffer. Upstream writes 0x3B4 in
+			 * new_trx_end, before this refill; that opens a window in
+			 * which the chip may DMA into the not-yet-refilled slot --
+			 * which still points at the skb already handed to
+			 * mac80211 -- and on a slow CPU under sustained RX it does,
+			 * silently scribbling that buffer. */
+			rtl_write_word(rtlpriv, 0x3B4,
+				       rtlpci->rx_ring[hw_queue].next_rx_rp);
 		} else {
 			if (!_rtl_pci_init_one_rxdesc(hw, skb, (u8 *)pdesc,
 						      rxring_idx,
